695 (2023) regarding UNIFIL's mandate renewal. The vote was 13 in favour, none against, with China and the Russian Federation abstaining. The mandate expires on 31 August 2024. Operative provisions confirm UNIFIL's independence in executing tasks without prior permission, while mandating continued coordination with Lebanon's Government under the status-of-forces agreement. China supported the mission's work but noted the text did not fully address Lebanon's concerns, emphasizing host-State sovereignty and consent. It advocated for closer communication between UNIFIL and Lebanese authorities. Russia attributed its abstention to contentious late drafting changes that lost a prior compromise. Despite this, Russia continued to support the mission's activities and called for coordination with the Lebanese Government. Both delegations agreed on the necessity of maintaining operational coordination with Lebanon, though China stressed sovereignty more explicitly while Russia focused on procedural compromises lost during drafting. Support for the mission remains distinct from endorsement of specific text provisions.", "input_tokens": 479, "output_tokens": 220, "termination": "complete"}}
